		"meta": {
			"author": "Stefan Mazur",
			"category": "source",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 23,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Rolling Landscape - Art Deco night skyline of the 1930s as parallax silhouettes. Works on any output: one projector, several projectors side by side or stacked, LED walls. Sizes are in scene units set by 'Scale' (1 = sized for a 1080 px high projector; use 2 for 2160 px), positions are relative to the frame edges (-1 = left / bottom, 1 = right / top), searchlights and airships are densities, so a wider or taller surface simply gets more of them. Nothing moves by itself: drive 'Clock' from Arena (Timeline or BPM Sync; play it backwards to scroll the other way). Physics: 'Parallax' sets how much slower the back layers move (0 = all equal, negative = back layers faster, above 1 the back layers move against the front). Skyline: 'Layer Count' 0-6 adds layers from back to front; fractional values fade the next layer in, so it can follow FFT smoothly. Layers 1-2: towers (stepped, crown with needle, mast, fan crown, slab). Layers 3-4: city (water tower, radio mast, theatre, department store, bridge pylon). Layers 5-6: street level (elevated railway with train, street lamps, power station, neon sign). 'Density': share of filled plots. 'Horizon': base line relative to the frame (-1 = bottom edge). 'Seed': a different value gives a different city. 'Layer 1-6 Color': one color per layer (Layer 1 = back). 'Window Lights': share of lit windows, 'Window Color' is used for all. Moon: 'Moon X' / 'Moon Y' relative to the frame (values beyond -1 / 1 place it off-screen; the moon sits behind the skyline, so animating Moon Y upwards gives a moonrise), 'Moon Opacity', 'Moon Size' (0 hides it), 'Moon Phase' (0 = new moon, 0.25 = first quarter, 0.5 = full, 0.75 = last quarter), 'Moon Ray Length' (1 = classic, 0 = no rays), 'Moon Color'. Searchlights: 'Beam Density' 0-1 (share of ground spots with a light, rising values fade new ones in, beams sweep with Clock), 'Beam Length', 'Beam Color'. Airships: 'Airship Density' 0-1 (they fly in rows over the whole sky and drift with Clock), 'Airship Dir' Left / Right / Random (Random picks a direction per row, changes with Seed), 'Airship Color'. Backdrop On/Off: colored sky or transparent. Drawn by the ISF shader RollingLandscape.fs in the patch folder (must stay next to the patch).",
			"displayName": "Rolling Landscape",
			"identifier": "3473280c-9853-4744-8083-c8dbbaba536b",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
